  "id": "basic-rule",
  "term": "basic rule",
  "definition": "In this source, the basic rule is that when the mammalian neocortex gets larger, it also becomes more folded. Larger brains tend to develop disproportionately more convolutions, although folding is not explained by size increase alone.",
